  "notes": "USAGE AS SURU-VERB: {対面|たいめん}する means \"to meet face-to-face.\" Example: {長年|ながねん}{会|あ}えなかった{父|ちち}と{対面|たいめん}した。(I met with my father, whom I hadn't seen for years.)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {対面|たいめん}する: to meet face-to-face\n- {対面|たいめん}での〜: in-person ~ (classes, meetings, etc.)\n- {初|はつ}{対面|たいめん}: first meeting\n- {感動|かんどう}の{対面|たいめん}: an emotional reunion\n\nMODERN USAGE: Since the COVID-19 pandemic, {対面|たいめん} has become widely used as a modifier meaning \"in-person\" as opposed to オンライン (online), as in {対面|たいめん}{授業|じゅぎょう} (in-person classes) vs. オンライン{授業|じゅぎょう} (online classes).",
